05-art77-scope	From 18 February 2027 each LMT battery, EV battery and industrial battery above 2 kWh placed on the market or put into service requires a battery passport with model and individual-battery data.	https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1542/2025-07-31/eng/	Article 77(1)-(2), lines 2846-2868	verified
05-qr-rule	From 18 February 2027 covered batteries require a QR code leading to the passport; marking must be visible, legible and indelible on the battery or, where appropriate, packaging/documents. The QR links to a placing-operator-assigned unique identifier and both must comply with the listed ISO/IEC 15459 family or equivalent.	https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1542/2025-07-31/eng/	Articles 13(6)-(7) and 77(3), lines 979-996 and 2881-2885	verified
05-second-life-transfer	For reused, repurposed or remanufactured batteries, passport responsibility transfers to the new placing operator and a new passport must link to the original passport(s); new status markings are also required.	https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1542/2025-07-31/eng/	Articles 13(9) and 77(7), lines 1001-1002 and 2897-2899	verified
05-operator-responsibility	The placing operator remains responsible for accurate, complete and current passport data even when another operator is authorised, and passport information must use open, interoperable, machine-readable formats without vendor lock-in.	https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1542/2025-07-31/eng/	Article 77(4)-(5), lines 2887-2895	verified
